# ── Supabase (optional) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Powers the "Sign in with Google" control in the navigation.
#
# Both values are safe to expose in a browser bundle — Supabase authorises
# every request with row-level security, not with a hidden key. Never put a
# service_role key here; that one must stay server-side.
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` (git-ignored) and fill it in.
# Leave both blank and the site still builds and runs: the sign-in control
# renders disabled with a "not configured" note.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# ── Razorpay (optional, server-side only) ──────────────────────────────
# Powers the "Pay ₹— · test mode" button in each product modal.
#
# These are NOT prefixed with VITE_, on purpose. Vite only inlines VITE_*
# variables into the browser bundle; these two stay on the server, inside the
# functions in `api/`, where the secret can actually be kept secret.
#
# Use TEST-MODE keys (rzp_test_…). Live keys would move real money.
# Get them from Razorpay dashboard → Account & Settings → API Keys →
# "Generate Test Key". No KYC documents are needed for test mode.
#
# Leave both blank and the site still builds and runs: the button renders as
# "Test payments not configured" and nothing else changes.

RAZORPAY_KEY_ID=
RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET=
